http://jsoc.stanford.edu/data/timed/index.html


M. Mierla et al.: Prominence eruption observed in He II 304 Å up to >6 R� by EUI/FSI aboard Solar Orbiter

for Imaging X-rays (STIX; Krucker et al. 2020), as shown in
Fig. A.2. The footpoints of the flare associated with this erup-
tion are most likely occulted by the limb as seen from STIX.
This means that the observed emission is most likely thermal
soft X-ray emission from the corona (perhaps with a small non-
thermal contribution), either from the flare arcade or from the
hottest part of the erupting CME. As the majority of the X-ray
emission is occulted, it is not possible to conclusively determine
the estimated GOES class from these observations. Further de-
tailed analysis of this event as observed by STIX will be pre-
sented in a separate paper.

